			"notes": "# Update v1.3\n\n## Additions\n### Items\n#### Warped Wart\n- Like Nether Wart, but warped.\n- Crafted with 1 Warped Wart Block in the Quartz Shredder, yielding 9.\n### Status Effects\n#### Immortality\n- Makes the user immune to all damage, similar to creative mode.\n- Potions can be found in End city chests.\n#### Overkill\n- The stronger the user's enemy is, the harder the user hits.\n- Potions can be found in stronghold chests and ancient city chests.\n#### Adamance\n- Lessens knockback.\n- Potions can be brewed with Steel Wool.\n#### Mercilessness\n- Perpetually increases the user's attack speed the more hits they land in quick succession.\n- Potions can be brewed with Warped Wart.\n#### Instant Death\n- Makes the next hit 20 times as strong, but has a 50/50 chance of that meaning either the user getting hit or the user hitting somebody.\n- Potions can be dropped rarely by Witches.\n#### Serenity\n- Makes all mobs within a certain radius of the user unable to target anything.\n- Potions can be brewed with Pink Petals.\n## Changes\n- Let the player uncraft their nether wart blocks by putting them through the Quartz Shredder.\n- Completely revamped the Quartz Shredder. It now has recipe support, RoughlyEnoughItems support, and a GUI.\n## Fixes\n- Rainbow eucalyptus wood was not flammable.\n- The Quartz Shredder would sometimes decrement the stack used to store the output of the recipe, causing you to make one less item until you restarted the game."
		},
